        "thought_text": "Re-evaluate the logic for determining if all doors can be unlocked. Since each door is controlled by exactly two switches, toggling either switch will affect the door's state. Therefore, the total number of toggles for each door must be even because each toggle by one switch is canceled out by a toggle by the other switch. Thus, the initial state of each door determines whether it can be unlocked regardless of the number of switches controlling it. If a door starts locked, it cannot be unlocked; if it starts unlocked, it remains unlocked. To determine if all doors can be unlocked, we need to check if the number of locked doors is even. If it is, then it is possible to unlock all doors by toggling the appropriate switches. Otherwise, it is not possible.",
